//
// One of THREE Model Broker services (Router + Gateway + Classifier).
// LOCKED Tier 2 D6: NEVER fold these three into a single binary (god-object reject).
//
// Gateway responsibility: actual model invocation execution. Caller passes the
// chosen_model_id from the Router (Gateway never picks fallbacks itself —
// fallback chain comes from RouteResponse). Gateway dispatches via the
// adapter pattern (Vertex AI / self-hosted Gemma / future provider) and
// performs:
//   - two-tier cache lookup (exact match + per-tenant semantic via pgvector)
//   - retry / fallback per Router-issued chain
//   - atomic TokenUsageLedger write per call (in chora_observability)
//   - OTLP span emission with OpenInference attributes (gen_ai.system,
//     llm.model_name, llm.token_count.{prompt,completion,total}, ...)
//   - per-tenant LoRA adapter loading when ModelDecision.adapter_uri set
//     (cross-tenant adapter loading FORBIDDEN — Tier 5 D19)
//
// Two RPC shapes:
//   - Invoke: synchronous unary (full completion in one response)
//   - InvokeStreaming: server-stream of chunks for token-streaming UX
//
// Cloud Run scale-to-zero in chora-489812 team-platform. mTLS via Cloud
// Service Mesh; SPIFFE identity in mesh; W3C trace context in gRPC metadata.
